desc:Star [Arcana synth] (GFX)
//tags: instrument synth virtual analogue 90s vst arpeggiator three arps lcr delay echo chorus phaser tremolo autopan arcana
//author: JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Requires gfx-drift, gfx-output, gfx-ui, gfx-panel, gfx-instrument and gfx-voice (.jsfx-inc) in the same folder.
//
// THE STAR (card XVII of the GFX Arcana series): hope, healing and renewed inspiration. A late-90s native soft synth -
// the bundled, lightweight virtual analogue that came free with the first generation of VST sequencers: two plain
// oscillators, one resonant low-pass, two envelopes, a little raw and a little aliased - poured out into three
// channels, LEFT, CENTRE and RIGHT, each with its own arpeggiator and its own delay unit, mixed back together under
// the star.
//
// THE SYNTH (one patch, played by all three channels)
//   OSC 1     SAW, SQUARE, TRIANGLE or SINE; OCTAVE (-2 .. +1).
//   OSC 2     the same waves; SEMI (-12 .. +12), DETUNE (cents).
//   MIX       OSC 1 .. OSC 2; PW (the squares' width); UNISON (each oscillator doubled and spread, 0 = off); DRIVE (into
//             the filter).
//   FILTER    a 2-pole resonant low-pass of the period (a state-variable): CUTOFF, RESO (to self-oscillation), ENV
//             (+/-), KEY (key tracking), VEL (velocity to the filter envelope).
//   FILTER ENV / AMP ENV   A, D, S, R sliders; VEL (velocity to the level).
//   LFO       RATE, to PITCH (vibrato) and to CUTOFF; GLIDE.
//   The oscillators are the plain kind (no band-limiting) run at twice the rate and folded down simply: bright,
//   a touch of grit in the top octave, as they were. RAW runs them (and the filter) at the host rate instead: rawer,
//   more aliased - and half the work.
// THREE CHANNELS: L, C, R. Every note you play goes to all three.
//   ARP       ON (lit: the channel arpeggiates the held chord; dark: it plays the chord as you hold it), MODE (UP, DOWN,
//             UP-DN, DN-UP, RANDOM, PLAYED, CHORD), RATE, OCT (1 - 4), GATE (10 - 200 %), TRANS (+/- 24 semitones),
//             OFFSET (start the channel's walk this many steps in, so the three interlock). LATCH (the header) holds the
//             chord. Locked to REAPER while it plays, free at the project tempo while it is stopped.
//   Each channel's DELAY UNIT, in signal order:
//   INPUT     HPF, LPF, DRIVE (- trims, + drives).
//   EQ        BASS, TREBLE (broad Baxandall shelves).
//   DELAY     TIME (tempo divisions, 1/32 .. 1/2), FEEDBACK (the repeats run through the input filters), MIX. The right
//             repeat sits a hair behind the left, so the echoes open out.
//   FX        SAT (tape saturation with its soft top), MOD (CHORUS or PHASER: AMOUNT, RATE), TREM (SINE or SQUARE:
//             DEPTH, RATE in tempo divisions), AUTO (PAN or VOLUME: DEPTH, RATE in bars).
//   OUTPUT    COMP (one knob: threshold down, ratio up, makeup in), WIDTH (0 - 200 %).
// MIXER  each channel's FADER and MUTE; SPREAD (how far L and R sit from the centre); TAPE <-> IRON (the master
//        stage's character: tape - soft, rounded, the top eased off; iron - a transformer's weight and grip in the
//        lows) and its DRIVE.
// FATE   the series' drift: each voice a little off pitch and drifting, each arpeggiated note a touch early or late.
// VOLUME, LEVEL, SAT (the output soft clip is always on).
// MIDI   notes (channel select), CC64 sustain, CC1 adds vibrato, CC120 / CC123 stop everything.

import gfx-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-ui.jsfx-inc
import gfx-panel.jsfx-inc
import gfx-instrument.jsfx-inc
import gfx-voice.jsfx-inc

